#!/usr/bin/env bash
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRACKED TOOLING. This script is version-controlled because it consumes
# tracked structured data: codex_migrate_class calls
# 'gen_migration_order.py --classify', which parses migration_plan.md.
# Tracking the generator and the plan but not their consumer would leave the
# interface unversioned on one side. See DESIGN_DECISIONS.md.
#
# NOT host-portable as-is. Host-specific assumptions:
#   repo path    /home/salatiel/work/infra_populi
#   SSH aliases  puppet8master, puppet8master-rsync, puppet8node
#   master paths /etc/puppetlabs/code/environments/production/...
#   params dir   ~/.config/infra_populi/params  (UNTRACKED: environment-specific
#                values, deliberately not versioned - see the tooling-tracking
#                decision in DESIGN_DECISIONS.md)
# Parameterizing these via environment variables is a known future improvement.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

set -euo pipefail

[[ $# -ge 1 ]] || { echo "Usage: codex_migrate_class <puppet_class_name>"; exit 2; }
CLASS="$1"

RUNBOOK="$HOME/.config/infra_populi/CODEX_RUNBOOK.md"
[[ -f "$RUNBOOK" ]] || { echo "Missing runbook: $RUNBOOK"; exit 2; }

cd /home/salatiel/work/infra_populi

codex exec \
  -c 'sandbox_mode="danger-full-access"' \
  -c 'approval_policy="never"' \
  "$(cat "$RUNBOOK")

TARGET CLASS: $CLASS

First action: run the harness:
~/.local/bin/infra_populi_tools/test_class.sh $CLASS

The injected runbook is authoritative: section 1 defines your authority, section 3 defines what stops you, and section 4 defines how to record a block.

TRACKER / ANNOTATION RULES (apply at commit time, in the same commit):
- In .codex_state/migrated_classes.txt, find the line for this class (the tracker uses SHORT names, e.g. 'backup_rsnapshot', with no puppet_infrastructure:: prefix) and mark it exactly: '<short_name> Done [from: release-0.9.8]'. Plain 'Done' is reserved for the 15 historical pre-baseline migrations - do NOT use it for new work.
- If the migration is NOT faithful to release-0.9.8 (deliberate divergence), stop and report instead of choosing a marker yourself.
- Do not force-add ignored trackers.

ORDER FILE REGENERATION:
- AFTER the migration commit lands, regenerate the order file: python3 .codex_state/gen_migration_order.py
- commit the regenerated .codex_state/migration_order.md (it is tracked; use 'git add -f' if git reports it ignored)
"
